   - The scheduler, not you, decides the day, the time and which meal a restaurant becomes, so a reason must stay true wherever the stop lands. Never mention a day of the week, a time of day (morning, dusk, night), a clock time, or a meal (breakfast, lunch, dinner, aperitivo). Say "a splurge" rather than "your splurge dinner".
 
